<title>BELGIUM: Luxembourg Cregem 96 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Luxembourg Cregem 96 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg-based  Cregem International Bank said in a statement on Monday that 1996 net profit rose 20 percent to 210 million Belgian francs. Total assets rose 14 percent to 86 billion francs.</p>
<p>Comparable figures were not given.</p>
<p>Cregem is a 100-percent unit of Credit Communal/Gemeentekrediet, the Belgian arm of the Belgian-French Dexia financial services group.</p>
<p>Cregem is destined to become the new group's private banking arm.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
